WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
At an Orthodox wedding, the priest
holds crowns above the bride and groom.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.650
In an English church, a
couple swap rings and promise:

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.090
for better for worse,
till death us do part.

4
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.800
At a graveside, a mourner throws
a handful of earth onto a coffin.

5
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.400
So what do rings, crowns and a handful of
earth say about what Christians believe?

6
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.880
In this mission, you'll
follow a wedding service,

7
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.130
and an Orthodox crowning, step by step.

8
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.700
Then you'll read words heard at funerals,

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.260
and see why churches differ
on burial and cremation.

10
00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:39.150
Your mission: explain what Christian
weddings and funerals show about love and

11
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:39.810
death.
